{
 "id": "lem-zl-relative-curve-mixedness",
 "blueprint": {
  "is": "lem-zl-relative-curve-mixedness",
  "from": null,
  "same_as": null
 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Mixedness of the direct images over a relative affine curve",
 "statement": "Fix the coefficient and weight conventions of\n[def-weil-punctual-weights]. Let $h:U_0\\to Y_0$ be a\nsmooth separated morphism\nbetween separated finite-type\n$k_0$-schemes, with every nonempty geometric fiber a smooth affine curve,\nand let $\\mathcal F$ be a\nlisse\n$\\Qlb$-Weil sheaf that is\npunctually $\\iota$-pure of weight\n$w$. Then for every $i$ there is a real number $u_i$ such that\n$R^ih_!\\mathcal F$ is\n$\\iota$-mixed of weights at most\n$u_i$.\nThe proof follows the reduction in Kiehl–Weissauer I.7, pp. 53–54:\nthe curve bound separates the two cohomological root radii, and\n[thm-zl-real-mixed-by-curves] supplies mixedness on the base by\ngeometric reduction to the already proved real-sheaf theorem on curves.\nNo instance of the general direct-image weight theorem is imported.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-p-dl-general-relative-line/lem-zl-relative-curve-mixedness.md",
  "place": "node lem-zl-relative-curve-mixedness, order 2843"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-weil-punctual-weights",
  "thm-zl-real-mixed-by-curves",
  "def-weil-pbc-constructible-complexes",
  "def-weil-pbc-qbar-category",
  "def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions",
  "def-weil-scheme-morphism-properties"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Normalize $\\mathcal F$ as in\n[def-wf-normalized-real-envelope]: put\n$b=\\iota^{-1}(q^{-w/2})$,\n$\\mathcal F^0=\\mathcal F\\otimes\\mathcal B_b$, and\n$\\mathcal E=\\mathcal F^0\\oplus(\\mathcal F^0)^\\vee$.\nIt is lisse, pure of weight zero and real by\n[lem-wf-envelope-real]. The relative factor calculation\n[lem-zl-relative-envelope-factor-reality], which uses only the\nproved curve estimate, shows that $R^ih_!\\mathcal E$ is real for\nevery $i$. These are constructible sheaves: the finite-level\nfiniteness theorem [sbc-thm-finiteness-finite-type] supplies the\nconstructible landing hypotheses in the coefficient passage of\n[thm-cbc-qbar].",
   "uses": [
    "def-wf-normalized-real-envelope",
    "lem-wf-envelope-real",
    "lem-zl-relative-envelope-factor-reality",
    "sbc-thm-finiteness-finite-type",
    "thm-cbc-qbar"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "Apply [thm-zl-real-mixed-by-curves] on $Y_0$, obtaining a\nfinite mixed filtration of $R^ih_!\\mathcal E$.\nAdditivity makes $R^ih_!\\mathcal F^0$ a direct summand, so it is\nmixed by [lem-a1-mixed-direct-summand]. The constant-twist\nprojection formula [lem-wf-constant-twist-cohomology] identifies\n\n$$\nR^ih_!\\mathcal F\n\\cong R^ih_!\\mathcal F^0\\otimes\\mathcal B_{b^{-1}}.\n$$",
   "uses": [
    "thm-zl-real-mixed-by-curves",
    "lem-a1-mixed-direct-summand",
    "lem-wf-constant-twist-cohomology"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "Tensoring the finite filtration with this rank-one sheaf is exact.\nAt a closed point of degree $m$, the twist multiplies each\neigenvalue by $b^{-m}$, of $\\iota$-modulus $q^{mw/2}$, by\n[def-wf-constant-weil-twist]. Thus every pure quotient of weight\n$v$ becomes pure of weight $v+w$, including where its stalk is\nzero. This gives the required finite mixed filtration without a\nlissity assumption on the direct image. Its finitely many\nweights have a maximum $u_i$; for the zero sheaf take any $u_i$.",
   "uses": [
    "def-wf-constant-weil-twist"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
